<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#Axis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The logical meaning of a dimension, independent of the dimension's extent or storage stride."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#Axis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#CellDataTypeRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One arm of a hasConditionalCellDataType list: a HEL condition and the cell type it selects."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#CellDataTypeRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#CellDataTypeRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:condition, dlv:ruleCellDataType. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#CellDataTypeRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of dlv:CellDataTypeRule Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#CellDataTypeRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cell Data Type Rule Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#CellDataTypeRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ChunkOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The order in which chunks appear in the chunk offset table."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ChunkOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ChunkedLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for dlv:chunkLengthsFromField, dlv:chunkOffsetBase, dlv:chunkOffsetsFromField, dlv:chunkOrder. A chunked dlv:DataLayout (any Dimension declaring dlv:chunkSize or dlv:chunkSizeFromField) must declare dlv:chunkOffsetsFromField."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ChunkedLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of dlv:DataLayout Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ChunkedLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Chunked Layout Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ChunkedLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DataLayout> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A declaration of how logical array cells are addressed in a physical byte region, including dimensions, strides, cell type and optional chunking."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DataLayout> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DataLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for dlv:cellBitWidth, dlv:cellBitWidthFromField, dlv:cellDataType, dlv:cellPackingOrder, dlv:hasConditionalCellDataType, dlv:hasConditionalDimensionOrder, dlv:hasDimension. Every member of a hasConditionalCellDataType list must be a dlv:CellDataTypeRule. Every member of a hasConditionalDimensionOrder list must be a dlv:DimensionOrderRule. dlv:cellPackingOrder is only meaningful with dlv:cellBitWidth or dlv:cellBitWidthFromField."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DataLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of dlv:DataLayout Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DataLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Data Layout Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DataLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#Dimension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One position in a data layout's ordered dimensions, with an extent, optional stride or chunk size, and optional axis meaning."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#Dimension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionOrderRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One arm of a hasConditionalDimensionOrder list: a HEL condition and the dimension order it selects."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionOrderRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionOrderRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:condition, dlv:ruleDimensionOrder. Every member of a ruleDimensionOrder list must be a dlv:Dimension."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionOrderRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of dlv:DimensionOrderRule Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionOrderRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dimension Order Rule Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionOrderRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for dlv:chunkSize, dlv:chunkSizeFromField, dlv:dimensionSize, dlv:dimensionSizeFromField, dlv:dimensionStride, dlv:dimensionStrideFromExpression, dlv:dimensionStrideFromField, dlv:hasAxis. A dlv:Dimension must use at most one stride mechanism (dimensionStride / dimensionStrideFromField / dimensionStrideFromExpression)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of dlv:Dimension Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dimension Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#DimensionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Namespace prefix declarations reused by SHACL SPARQL constraints and rules. This is validation infrastructure, not a property of parsed data."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Used by named SHACL SPARQL constraints/rules in this module. Not intended for instance-data assertions."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "prefixes"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisBand> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The axis indexing separate bands or channels of a multi-component array."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisBand> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisBand> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The temporal axis of a layout; sample spacing and time reference must be described separately."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The logical horizontal or first spatial coordinate axis of a layout."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisX> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The logical vertical-in-grid or second spatial coordinate axis of a layout; ground-coordinate direction is specified separately."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisY> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisZ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The third spatial coordinate axis of a layout."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisZ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#axisZ> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#cellBitWidth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bits each cell occupies in the packed stream, when that is not the cell type's intrinsic width. Cells are contiguous in the bit stream and may straddle byte boundaries; a cell type is still required, to say how the bits are interpreted. Absent means cells occupy their type's natural width."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#cellBitWidth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#cellBitWidthFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Field whose parsed value is the packed cell width in bits. GRIB2 carries this in its data-representation section, so the width is a property of the message rather than of the format."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#cellBitWidthFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#cellDataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The datatype of a single array cell before any conditional cell-type rule is applied."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#cellDataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#cellPackingOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Whether the first cell of a byte occupies its most or least significant bits. Default bddo:MSBFirst, which is what GRIB2, NITF and the 1-bit and 4-bit image formats all use; LSB-first packing exists but is rare. Only meaningful alongside dlv:cellBitWidth."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#cellPackingOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkLengthsFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The repeating Field holding each chunk's byte length (e.g. TIFF TileByteCounts). Required when chunks are individually encoded; when absent, a chunk's length is its cell count times the cell width."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkLengthsFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkOffsetBase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What the chunk offsets are relative to. Default bddo:streamStart."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkOffsetBase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkOffsetsFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The repeating Field holding each chunk's byte offset, indexed in chunkOrder (e.g. TIFF TileOffsets, NITF block offsets)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkOffsetsFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Traversal order of the chunk offset table. Default dlv:rowMajor (chunks vary fastest along the fastest-varying dimension)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkSize> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Extent of one chunk (tile/block) along this dimension, in cells. When any Dimension of a DataLayout declares a chunk extent, the layout is chunked: the grid is partitioned into chunks of this shape and each chunk is located through the layout's chunk offset table. A trailing partial chunk is padded to the full chunk extent. A Dimension of a chunked layout that declares neither dlv:chunkSize nor dlv:chunkSizeFromField is chunked at its full extent, i.e. its chunk extent is its dlv:dimensionSize (or the value read through dlv:dimensionSizeFromField); a layout chunked on X alone therefore has chunks spanning all of Y. Within a chunked layout, dlv:dimensionStride addresses cells inside one chunk, not across the whole grid."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkSize> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkSizeFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The field whose parsed value supplies the number of cells per chunk along a dimension."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#chunkSizeFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#columnMajor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Chunk enumeration convention in which the first logical dimension varies fastest."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#columnMajor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#columnMajor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionSize> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The fixed number of cells along a physical-layout dimension."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionSize> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionSizeFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The field whose parsed value supplies a layout dimension's extent."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionSizeFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionStride> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bytes to advance per step along this dimension (pitch), as a fixed literal. When no stride is declared by any mechanism, addressing is contiguous (stride = size of the next-faster block). Stride stays in BYTES even for a bit-packed layout: rows of a packed grid are normally padded to a byte boundary while the cells within a row are not, so the pitch is whole bytes and dlv:cellBitWidth governs only the packing inside one row."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionStride> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionStrideFromExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A HEL expression giving this dimension's stride in bytes. Use when the pitch is computed rather than stored -- BMP's row padding is ((width * bitsPerPixel + 31) / 32) * 4 with HEL integer division (nonnegative integer operands; overflow is an error), which no literal can express. Mirrors dimensionSize/dimensionSizeFromField: a lone sibling name takes the FromField form, anything else this one."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionStrideFromExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionStrideFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Field whose parsed value is this dimension's stride in bytes. Use when the pitch is carried in the format rather than fixed, e.g. an explicit row-bytes header field."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#dimensionStrideFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hasAxis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The logical axis assigned to a physical-layout dimension; it does not itself establish byte order."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hasAxis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hasConditionalCellDataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered rdf:List of CellDataTypeRule. The first rule whose condition holds gives the layout's cell type. Mutually exclusive with dlv:cellDataType."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hasConditionalCellDataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hasConditionalDimensionOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered rdf:List of DimensionOrderRule. The first rule whose condition holds gives the layout's dimension order. Each rule names the SAME Dimension nodes in a different sequence -- band interleaving is a permutation of axes, not a different set of them. Mutually exclusive with dlv:hasDimension."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hasConditionalDimensionOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hasDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered rdf:List of dimensions, slowest- to fastest-varying."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hasDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hilbert> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Chunk traversal following a Hilbert space-filling order; the profile/processor must identify the applicable dimension and boundary convention."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hilbert> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#hilbert> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#morton> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Chunk traversal ordered by interleaving coordinate bits into a Morton or Z-order key; the profile/processor must agree on dimensionality and bounds."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#morton> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#morton> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#rowMajor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Chunk enumeration convention in which the last logical dimension varies fastest."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#rowMajor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#rowMajor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ruleCellDataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The cell datatype selected when the associated conditional rule matches."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ruleCellDataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ruleDimensionOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The ordered rdf:List of dlv:Dimension selected by a DimensionOrderRule, slowest- to fastest-varying."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#ruleDimensionOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
